---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Learning — GrabStack" description="What to learn, and in what order — courses, programmes and concepts mapped to the competency you need.">
  <section class="py-6 sm:py-10">
    <h1 class="font-sans text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
      Learning<span class="text-accent">.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-xl text-base text-muted">
      What to learn, and in what order — courses, programmes and concepts mapped to the competency you need.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="space-y-4">
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-white/10 bg-surface p-6">
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper/80">
        Learning tracks are organised by competency — what to learn, with what tools, in what order.
        Each track carries a date so you know it's current.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">
        We're assembling the first tracks now. Check <a href="/wire" class="text-accent hover:underline">The Wire</a> for updates.
      </p>
    </div>

    <a href="/learning/agent-taxonomy" class="group block rounded-lg border border-white/10 bg-surface p-5 transition-colors hover:border-white/20">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-paper group-hover:text-accent transition-colors">Agent Taxonomy</h3>
      <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted">A faceted taxonomy of AI agents — types, access levels, and how they differ.</p>
    </a>
  </div>
</Base>
